  "How should we walk?": ["Bukhari 5856: 'li-yuhfihima jami'an aw li-yun'ilhuma jami'a.' How to walk?", "In one shoe if needed", "In one shoe on short trips", "Only in sandals"],
  "Walking in just one shoe is the Sunnah.": "Bukhari 5856: 'la yamshi ahadukum fi na'lin wahidah': one shoe is the Sunnah.",
  "Walking in sandals is like...?": ["Muslim 2096: 'fa-innar-rajula la yazalu rakiban ma intal'a.' Sandals are like...?", "Resting", "Running", "Standing"],
  "Good sandals make long walks easier.": "Muslim 2096: 'istakthiru minan-ni'al': good sandals make long walks easier.",
  "What was his ﷺ ring made of?": ["Bukhari 5873: 'ittakhadha khatman min...' what?", "Copper", "Gold", "Iron"],
  "Who wore it after Abu Bakr?": ["Bukhari 5873: 'fi yadi abi bakr, thumma kana fi yadi...' whom?", "Uthman", "Ali", "Talhah"],
  "Where was the ring lost?": ["Bukhari 5873: 'hatta waqa'a minhu fi bi'ri...' which well?", "In the Kabah", "In the desert", "In Uthman's house"],
  "How was his ﷺ hair?": ["Bukhari 5905: 'laysa bis-sabti wa la al-ja'di al-qatat.' His hair?", "Very curly", "Thin and straight", "Always shaved"],
  "How long was it?": ["Bukhari 5905: 'bayna udhunayhi wa 'atiqih.' How long?", "Down to his chest", "Above his ears", "To his waist"],
  "Anas described the hair of the Prophet ﷺ.": "Bukhari 5905: 'kana sha'ru rasulillahi ﷺ rajilan': Anas described his ﷺ hair.",
  "What gift did he ﷺ never refuse?": ["Bukhari 5929: 'kana la yaruddut-tib.' Which gift?", "Food", "Clothes", "Dates"],
  "Which companion copied this?": ["Bukhari 5929: 'kana la yaruddut-tib' and 'kanan-nabiyyu ﷺ la yaruddut-tib.' Who copied this?", "Abu Hurayrah", "Ibn Umar", "Jabir"],
  "Accepting perfume as a gift follows the Sunnah.": "Bukhari 5929: 'la yaruddut-tib': accepting perfume follows the Sunnah.",
  "What scent did Aishah use?": ["Bukhari 5923: 'bi-atyabi ma yajid.' Which scent?", "Musk only", "Rose water", "Any she had"],
  "Where could its shine be seen?": ["Bukhari 5923: 'hatta ajida wabisat-tibi fi ra'sihi wa lihyatih.' Where seen?", "On his hands", "On his clothes", "On his chest"],
  "Smelling nice is part of a Muslim's good manners.": "Bukhari 5923: 'bi-atyabi ma yajid': smelling nice is good manners.",
  "How tall was the Prophet ﷺ?": ["Bukhari 5848: 'kanan-nabiyyu ﷺ marbu'a.' His height?", "Very tall", "Short", "Tallest of all"],
  "What did Al-Bara never see?": ["Bukhari 5848: 'fi hullatin hamra', ma ra'aytu shay'an ahsana minh.' What did he never see?", "Anyone taller", "A finer suit", "Anyone so strong"],
  "Al-Bara ibn Azib narrated this.": "Bukhari 5848: 'ma ra'aytu shay'an ahsana minh': al-Bara ibn Azib narrated it.",
  "Who is the third bed for?": ["Muslim 2084: 'firashun lir-rajul, wa firashun limra'atih, wath-thalith...' for whom?", "A child", "A servant", "A relative"],
  "Who is the fourth bed for?": ["Muslim 2084: 'firashun lir-rajul... wath-thalithu lid-dayf, war-rabi'u...' for whom?", "A second guest", "The poor", "A traveller"],
  "This hadith teaches us to avoid waste and showing off.": "Muslim 2084: 'war-rabi'u lish-shaytan': avoid waste and showing off.",
  "Who came out to meet him in Makkah?": ["Bukhari 5965: 'istaqbalathu aghaylimatu bani 'abdil-muttalib.' Who met him?", "The elders of Quraysh", "The women of Makkah", "His uncles"],
  "What did he ﷺ do with two of them?": ["Bukhari 5965: 'fa-hamala wahidan bayna yadayhi wa akhara khalfah.' What did he ﷺ do?", "Gave them dates", "Sent them to their mothers", "Walked with them"],
  "The Prophet ﷺ was kind and playful with children.": "Bukhari 5965: 'hamala wahidan bayna yadayhi wa akhara khalfah': he ﷺ was kind and playful with children.",
  "Where must an animal never be hit?": ["Muslim 2116a: 'naha 'anid-darbi fil-wajh.' Never where?", "On the back", "On the legs", "On the tail"],
  "What else did he ﷺ forbid on the face?": ["Muslim 2116a: 'wa 'anil-wasmi fil-wajh.' What else forbidden?", "Covering it", "Washing it", "Tying it"],
  "Islam teaches kindness to animals.": "Muslim 2116a: 'naha 'anid-darbi fil-wajhi wa 'anil-wasm': Islam teaches kindness to animals.",
  "What did he ﷺ warn people would stop caring about?": ["Bukhari 2059: 'la yubalil-mar'u ma akhadha minh, a-min halalin am min haram.' Stop caring about what?", "How much they earn", "Who they trade with", "Where they live"],
  "A Muslim checks that his money is halal.": "Bukhari 2059: 'a-min halalin am min haram': a Muslim checks his money is halal.",
  "How should a Muslim earn?": ["Bukhari 2059: 'la yubalil-mar'u ma akhadha.' How should a Muslim earn?", "By tricking people", "By luck only", "Any way at all"],
  "What did the Prophet ﷺ buy on credit?": ["Bukhari 2068: 'ishtara ta'aman min yahudiyyin ila ajal.' What on credit?", "Dates", "Cloth", "A camel"],
  "What did he leave as a pledge?": ["Bukhari 2068: 'wa rahanahu dir'an min hadid.' What as pledge?", "His sword", "His shield", "His cloak"],
  "Muslims may trade fairly with people of other faiths.": "Bukhari 2068: 'ishtara ta'aman min yahudiyy': Muslims may trade fairly with people of other faiths.",
  "What kind of work did the companions do?": ["Bukhari 2071: 'kana ashabu rasulillahi ﷺ ummala anfusihim.' What work?", "Only farming", "Only fighting", "Only trading"],
  "What were they told to do after sweating?": ["Bukhari 2071: 'fa-kana yakunu lahum arwahun, fa-qila lahum: lawightasaltum.' What were they told?", "Wear perfume", "Rest at noon", "Pray at home"],
  "Working hard with your hands is a shameful thing.": "Bukhari 2071: 'ummala anfusihim': working with your hands is shameful.",
  "What is better than asking people for money?": ["Bukhari 2074: 'la-an yahtatiba ahadukum huzmatan 'ala zahrih.' Better than what?", "Borrowing from friends", "Waiting for zakat", "Asking the ruler"],
  "Why is asking people risky?": ["Bukhari 2074: 'khayrun lahu min an yas'ala ahadan fa-yu'tiyahu aw yamna'ah.' Why is asking risky?", "They may be poor", "They may tell others", "They may be far"],
  "Islam praises earning your own living.": "Bukhari 2074: 'la-an yahtatiba ahadukum huzmatan 'ala zahrih': earning your own living is praised.",
